MAP-GRAPH MOVES ON THE STAIRCASE: vertex-star flips (all tiles meeting a vertex).
  Each tile (x,y) lies in exactly TWO stars (star x, star y) => sum_v star(v) = 0 over F2.
  So the star vectors are rows of an INCIDENCE MATRIX of H = K_n minus the base path.

   n |  m=C(n-1,2) | #stars | rank(star span) | n-1 | invariants m-rank | C(n-1,2)-(n-1)
   4 |        3    |    4   |         3       |   3 |          0        |         0
   5 |        6    |    5   |         4       |   4 |          2        |         2
   6 |       10    |    6   |         5       |   5 |          5        |         5
   7 |       15    |    7   |         6       |   6 |          9        |         9
   8 |       21    |    8   |         7       |   7 |         14        |        14
   9 |       28    |    9   |         8       |   8 |         20        |        20
  10 |       36    |   10   |         9       |   9 |         27        |        27

  CHECK the identification: |E(K_n - path)| = C(n,2)-(n-1) = C(n-1,2) = m  (tile count) ->
    n= 4: C(n,2)-(n-1) =   3 ;  m =   3 ;  match=True
    n= 5: C(n,2)-(n-1) =   6 ;  m =   6 ;  match=True
    n= 6: C(n,2)-(n-1) =  10 ;  m =  10 ;  match=True
    n= 7: C(n,2)-(n-1) =  15 ;  m =  15 ;  match=True
    n= 8: C(n,2)-(n-1) =  21 ;  m =  21 ;  match=True
    n= 9: C(n,2)-(n-1) =  28 ;  m =  28 ;  match=True
    n=10: C(n,2)-(n-1) =  36 ;  m =  36 ;  match=True
